}}

==Enemy==
Red EnerG is one hell of a support enemy, boasting 370 range, at least 680k health in Uncanny and Zero Legends and only 3 knockbacks. At that point, he has slightly over 3 times of H. Nah's health with less damage per hit (18,303 vs 13,580), but his 100% chance to create a Lv.2 [[Surge Attack]] more than makes up for that. His knockback ability can synergize with the Surge to create a near-impenetrable wall that essentially counters rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. On top of that, the Surge extends his attacks to a maximum of 475 range, meaning most non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] Cats will never be completely safe.

==Strategy==
The Surge mostly invalidates the sync + [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] strategy commonly used on H. Nah, so [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] is your best bet to chain this monstrosity with her Surge Immunity, unless Bahamut's [[Explosion]] talent has been unlocked, which gives him the burst of damage needed to repeatedly stagger Red EnerG. You can bait out Red EnerG's initial attack with fast units such as Bullet Train Cat to allow Idi:N2 to safely land a hit. It is ideal to chain Red EnerG with both Awakened Bahamut and Idi:N2 to quickly end the fight against him. Take note that while [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]] is not very reliable against this foe due to a lack of Surge Immunity, it is still wise to bring Cutter for its [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Attack UP Combo]] with [[Li'l Axe Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Brave Cat]], and any damage you deal to Red EnerG is invaluable either way.

When accompanied by other frontliners such as [[Lord Gravey]], you can duke it out on Red EnerG from safety with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] such as [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. This is your safest method to slowly kill him without the risk of your cats walking into his dangerous Surges. [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]] or other longer-ranged units can also work due if they somehow stand outside his Surge distance. If you happen to have other [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]] able to deal meaningful damage to him, you can consider using them.

[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is fast enough to hit Red EnerG before dying as a quick and cheap burst of damage. [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]] can be used in a desperate situation as he can strike Red EnerG once before getting hit if no units are in the way, although he is helpless against the Surges.

With his Surge Immunity [[Talents|Talent]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] becomes highly effective at stalling this foe, and his slow speed helps to clog up the battlefield against Red EnerG's favor. Meatshields with the Dodge ability can also halt his progress for a good while, particularly Talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] and [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]]. The latter also has a Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] Talent, allowing her to work especially well in Red EnerG's debut stage, [[Burning Sunset]]. However, Dodge-only meatshields can be rather unreliable and will fall easily if they don't dodge. You might want to try [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] with Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]] instead, due to its Surge and Knockback Immunities preventing Red EnerG from pushing for a brief second.

A Talented [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] may seem appealing due to his Knockback Immunity. However, while he's fast and can clog up the field to ensure Red EnerG does not advance, the Surges will tear through his health quickly, which isn't ideal for such an expensive meatshield.

Notably, you can get [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] to freeze Red EnerG if it has a minimum Move Speed Talent level of 5 by catching Red EnerG after the Surge ends, which gives you a little more breathing room. Due to iCat's long recharge time, it is unlikely for you to actually be able to stack them, so you will have to rely on Combos in order to perma-freeze Red EnerG or just forgo this option entirely and save your slots for something else.

